  ($c$conceptual-framework-information-kiosk-western-rajasthan$c$, $c$Conceptual Framework of Information Kiosk in Western Rajasthan$c$, $c$D. Kumar, R. S. Mehta, A. Patidar, S. C. Meena$c$, $c$An interactive kiosk is a computer terminal with specialized software and hardware to provide access to information, services, or transactions. Initially resembling telephone booths, kiosks now serve in retail, food service, hospitality, and other sectors.$c$, $c$<p>An interactive kiosk is a computer terminal with specialized software and hardware to provide access to information, services, or transactions. Initially resembling telephone booths, kiosks now serve in retail, food service, hospitality, and other sectors.</p>
<figure><img src="/articles/vol-1-issue-1/image12.webp" alt="Conceptual Framework of Information Kiosk in Western Rajasthan" loading="lazy"></figure>
<figure><img src="/articles/vol-1-issue-1/image13.webp" alt="" loading="lazy"></figure>
<p><strong>Features:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Touchscreen interface</li>
<li>Smart buying and selling options</li>
<li>Increases awareness among farmers</li>
<li>Print-on-demand for information</li>
<li>Self-service reduces waiting times and staff requirements</li>
<li>Virtual sales assistance</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Implementation Steps:</strong></p>
<ol>
